# keys (M9): the plane's keys (CartesianPlane.test.tsx: "pans one grid square per arrow, zooms
# through the stops, 0 resets"; FV 07). A click on the empty plane (700, 600 at 1440 x 900) focuses
# it, as a press focuses the focusable plane under it (no ring: the pointer's focus), and the
# pointer leaves for the gap beside the panel (482, 500), so Q goes. → and ↑ pan one minor grid
# square each (0.5 at 50 px a unit): the view moves right and up, the origin from (468, 396) to
# (443, 421) in the plane; + steps the zoom to the next stop, 62.5 px a unit (125 %); − twice to 40
# (80 %); + with Alt held is the browser's and changes nothing; 0 resets the view (D17's 50, the
# origin centred); ] and [ move P along the curve by 0.1 (FunctionViewer.tsx's own keys, which the
# plane hands its owner first): P (2.10, 4.41), then twice back, P (1.90, 3.61).
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
click 700 600
move 482 500
wait 500
shot focused
key ArrowRight
key ArrowUp
wait 16
shot panned
key +
wait 16
shot in
key -
key -
wait 16
shot out
key + alt
wait 16
shot alt
key 0
wait 16
shot reset
key ]
wait 16
shot p-right
key [
key [
wait 16
shot p-left
